<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">09072026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Explosions struck four Iranian port cities on Wednesday as Washington declared the ceasefire over and demanded unfettered passage through the Strait of Hormuz.</s> <s>That waterway carries a fifth of the world's oil, and Brent crude jumped more than four percent to a two-week high while the Dow fell eight hundred points.</s> <s>Trump has now threatened to seize Kharg Island, the hub for ninety percent of Iran's oil exports.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Britain's next prime minister may be chosen by eighty-one lawmakers, not by voters.</s> <s>Labour's rulebook lets a candidate advance on the nomination of just twenty percent of its four hundred and three members of parliament, and after Keir Starmer resigned, Greater Manchester mayor Andy Burnham stands as the only declared contender.</s> <s>He could enter Downing Street by the twentieth of July, an ascent no ballot box will have decided.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Korea's ruling Democratic Party has fractured into a four-way leadership contest after former prime minister Kim Min-seok confirmed his bid.</s> <s>The race pits factions loyal to President Lee Jae-myung against a rival camp, testing whether a sitting president can still command his own party machine.</s> <s>Whether Lee's grip holds will decide how much of his agenda survives.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israel's military has cut the water to Al-Forat farm and begun sealing the Jordan Valley off from the rest of the occupied West Bank.</s> <s>The first twenty-two kilometres of a planned five-hundred-kilometre barrier now cut Palestinian families in Tubas from some of their most fertile farmland, with nineteen more phases mapped across the eastern West Bank.</s> <s>Dispossession here is not a byproduct of development... it is the development.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Indonesia has agreed to buy the supersonic BrahMos cruise missile from India, a deal Prime Minister Modi finalized during his visit to Jakarta.</s> <s>The world's largest Muslim-majority nation is diversifying its arsenal away from Russia and the West, while India breaks into an arms-export market those powers long dominated.</s> <s>Two Global South giants are quietly building a defence axis outside the Western supply chain.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In the mountains of Michoacán, cartels have turned illegal logging into a weapon against one of nature's great migrations.</s> <s>Tens of millions of monarch butterflies winter in a single sacred fir forest after travelling three thousand miles from Canada, and some local guardians have died defending the groves from armed loggers clearing land for cash crops.</s> <s>Organized crime has become an environmental actor, converting protected habitat into profit with impunity.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Russia's foreign minister Sergey Lavrov met his Mozambican counterpart in Maputo, the third stop on an Africa tour that has already taken him through Ethiopia and Niger.</s> <s>Moscow is trading arms, security deals, and debt relief for diplomatic cover across a continent increasingly willing to play great powers against one another.</s> <s>What minerals and loyalties it locks in now may outlast the war that made it a pariah in the West.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Across Japan, South Korea, and China, a growing share of young people have simply stopped looking for work, and the official jobless figures never count them.</s> <s>Economists call them NEET, youth neither in employment, education, nor training, and because they exit the labour force rather than register as unemployed, the true scale stays hidden.</s> <s>A broken bargain between schooling and opportunity is quietly hollowing out East Asia's next generation.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Western Europe has just endured its hottest June on record, and roughly four thousand seven hundred excess deaths followed the heat.</s> <s>Average temperatures reached twenty point seven degrees Celsius, more than three degrees above the long-term norm, and Spain and Portugal are already gripped by a fourth heatwave.</s> <s>Record heat is now colliding with grids, water systems, and railways built for a cooler century.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Typhoon Bavi is roughly as wide as France, some one thousand kilometres across, drawing its size from record-warm Pacific waters.</s> <s>It would be the largest storm to threaten the region since nineteen eighty-seven, skirting northern Taiwan before it makes landfall in China's Fujian province this weekend, God willing weakening before it does.</s> <s>The same ocean heat driving Europe's records is now supercharging the storms of the Pacific.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>On the island of Tasmania, the crops depend on bees no one can protect.</s> <s>Beekeepers can medicate their managed hives against the Varroa mite, but the feral colonies that quietly pollinate much of the state cannot be treated, and the mite is already devastating mainland Australia.</s> <s>Should it cross the water, farmers would watch their harvests fail through a door they have no way to close.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Deep beneath the Indian Ocean near Amsterdam Island, the seafloor spread four point two metres in just six days.</s> <s>Instruments captured a magma reservoir draining beneath the ridge, producing some one hundred and fifty million cubic metres of new ocean floor, and much of that spreading left no seismic trace at all.</s> <s>If the Earth can remake itself in silence, our forecasts of where it will move next grow harder still.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Taiwan has draped netting over its anti-aircraft guns to protect them from the very drones they were built to destroy.</s> <s>The air force wrapped its twenty-four Swiss-made Skyguard cannons in mesh after cheap first-person-view drones began diving directly onto them.</s> <s>When a weapon worth millions needs a net against a machine worth hundreds, the economics of warfare have inverted.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>French investigators questioned Telegram's founder Pavel Durov for six hours in Paris, his fourth session nearly two years after his arrest.</s> <s>He faces charges of complicity in the platform's use for organized crime, punishable by up to ten years, though his lawyers say no supporting evidence has surfaced.</s> <s>At stake is a sweeping legal idea, that the creator of an encrypted network can be held personally criminal for whatever its users do.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Greece, victims of the Predator spyware have sued its maker, Intellexa, in a case that could set a global precedent.</s> <s>Traces of the surveillance tool surfaced on dozens of phones in twenty twenty-two, toppling the country's intelligence chief and the prime minister's chief of staff.</s> <s>A verdict against the company would be the first time a commercial spyware maker is held to account in a courtroom.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>